module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.KoszulCechHomotopyColimitCoprojections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.DerivedHomHomotopyColimitProjections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.KoszulPerfectDual

/-!
# The Koszul formula of Tag 0A0E with its projections pinned, and its cone along the unit

`KoszulPerfectDual.lean` proves [Stacks, Tag 0A0E]: the Čech completion `K^∧` of an object `K` of
`D(𝒪)` along the ideal sheaf generated by global sections `f_1, …, f_r` is a derived limit of the
tower `n ↦ K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 (K^n)^∨`. `CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.IsDerivedLimit` quantifies over the
structural map of its Milnor triangle, so which cone that triangle carries cannot be read off the
statement — and every comparison of two derived-limit presentations of one tower needs the cone.

This file supplies the presentation **with its projections named**, and computes its cone along
the completion unit.

* the projections are the maps `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(Q(K^n) ⟶ Q(Č(f)), K)` induced by the canonical
  comparisons `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.koszulCechComplexMap` of [Stacks, Tag 0913], read
  through `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.koszulTensorDualSystemIso`. Nothing is existentially
  bound: this is [Stacks, Tag 0CRH] in the form
  `CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.IsHomotopyColimitWithCoprojections` applied to the Čech
  presentation of `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite`
  `.exists_isHomotopyColimitWithCoprojections_koszulPowerSystem`, whose coprojections are those
  very comparisons, followed by
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedLimitWithProjections_derivedSheafHom_of_coprojections`
  ([Stacks, Tag 0A0A] pinned) and the transport of projections along an isomorphism of towers;
* the composite of the completion unit `K ⟶ K^∧` with the `n`-th projection is the map which the
  single map of complexes `K^n ⟶ 𝒪[0]`

  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.koszulCechComplexMap X f n ≫ AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite`
  `.cechAugmentation X f`

  induces on derived internal Hom into `K`, after the identification `K = R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪, K)`.
  Neither the Čech complex nor the homotopy colimit survives in that expression.

The second point is what an argument identifying these projections with the canonical maps onto a
quotient tower consumes: by the uniqueness clause of a factorization through a derived-complete
object, a map out of `K^∧` is determined by its restriction along the unit, so pinning
`η ≫ π_n` is pinning `π_n`.

## Main results

* `RingedSite.isDerivedLimitWithProjections_tensorDerivedDualSystem_koszulPowerSystem_completion`
  — **[Stacks, Tag 0A0E] with the projections of its derived limit named.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionUnit_app_comp_map_koszulCechComplexMap` — the
  completion unit followed by the map induced by the Koszul–Čech comparison is the map induced by
  that comparison composed with the Čech augmentation.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionUnit_app_comp_tensorDerivedDualSystem_π` — **the cone of
  the pinned presentation along the completion unit**, the two previous results combined.

## Implementation notes

`CategoryTheory.Functor.flip` is used to state a projection, because
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedLimitWithProjections_derivedSheafHom_of_coprojections` is
stated through `(derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).flip.obj K`, while
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionUnit` is stated through
`(derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).map _ |>.app K`. The two are definitionally equal — `Functor.flip`
sends a morphism to the component of its image at the fixed object — and the crossing is made by
`congrArg` in term mode, which unifies at default transparency where `rw` does not.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0913](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0913)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0A](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0A)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0E)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CRH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CRH)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated Opposite

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

universe u

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard
attribute [-instance] Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.moduleSheavesAbelian
attribute [-instance] Stacks.DerivedTensor.ResolutionByExtensionsByZero.instAbelian

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})
  [HasSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [HasWeakSheafify X.J CommRingCat.{u}] {r : ℕ}
  (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0A0E] with the projections of its derived limit named.** The Čech completion
`K^∧ = R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(Č(f), K)` of [Stacks, Tag 099B] is a derived limit of the tower
`n ↦ K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 (K^n)^∨` **through** the maps which the canonical comparisons
`Q(K^n) ⟶ Q(Č(f))` of [Stacks, Tag 0913] induce on derived internal Hom into `K`, read through
the identification `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.koszulTensorDualSystemIso` of the tower with
`n ↦ R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(K^n, K)`.

`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_tensorDerivedDualSystem_koszulPowerSystem_completion`
is this statement with the projections forgotten. The strengthening is what any comparison of two
derived-limit presentations of one tower needs, since
`CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.IsDerivedLimit` existentially binds the structural map of its
Milnor triangle.

Three inputs, each unconditional: the Čech presentation of the Koszul system as a homotopy colimit
**with its coprojections named as the canonical comparisons**
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_isHomotopyColimitWithCoprojections_koszulPowerSystem`,
[Stacks, Tag 0913] followed by [Stacks, Tag 0CRH]); the direct-sum comparison
`R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(⊕ K^n, K) ≅ ∏ R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(K^n, K)` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_derivedSheafHomSigmaComparison`; and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.koszulTensorDualSystemIso`, whose being an isomorphism of towers
gives it eventual inverses at every level with `m = n`. -/
public theorem isDerivedLimitWithProjections_tensorDerivedDualSystem_koszulPowerSystem_completion
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))
    [HasCoproduct ((koszulPowerSystem X f ⋙ DerivedCategory.Q).obj)]
    [HasProduct fun n : ℕ ↦ (derivedSheafHomSystem X
      (koszulPowerSystem X f ⋙ DerivedCategory.Q) K).obj (op n)]
    [HasProduct fun n : ℕ ↦ (tensorDerivedDualSystem X
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.canonicalDerivedTensorProduct X)
      (koszulPowerSystem X f ⋙ DerivedCategory.Q) K).obj (op n)] :
    NoetherianAdicCompletion.IsDerivedLimitWithProjections
      (tensorDerivedDualSystem X (Stacks.SheafOfModules.canonicalDerivedTensorProduct X)
        (koszulPowerSystem X f ⋙ DerivedCategory.Q) K)
      ((completionFunctor X f).obj K)
      (fun n : ℕ ↦ ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).flip.obj K).map
            (DerivedCategory.Q.map (koszulCechComplexMap X f n)).op ≫
          (koszulTensorDualSystemIso X f K).inv.app (op n)) := by
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := exists_isHomotopyColimitWithCoprojections_koszulPowerSystem X f
  exact NoetherianAdicCompletion.IsDerivedLimitWithProjections.comp_of_hasEventualInverses
    (koszulTensorDualSystemIso X f K).inv
    (fun n ↦ ⟨n, le_rfl, (koszulTensorDualSystemIso X f K).hom.app (op n),
      by simpa using (koszulTensorDualSystemIso X f K).inv_hom_id_app (op n),
      by simpa using (koszulTensorDualSystemIso X f K).hom_inv_id_app (op n)⟩)
    (isDerivedLimitWithProjections_derivedSheafHom_of_coprojections X
      (koszulPowerSystem X f ⋙ DerivedCategory.Q) K
      (isIso_derivedSheafHomSigmaComparison X _ K) hc)

/-- **The completion unit followed by the map induced by the Koszul–Čech comparison is induced by
one map of complexes `K^n ⟶ 𝒪[0]`**, namely that comparison followed by the Čech augmentation.

The completion unit `K ⟶ K^∧` is the identification `K = R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪, K)` followed by the map
which the augmentation `Č(f) ⟶ 𝒪[0]` induces (`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionUnit_app`),
and derived internal Hom is a functor in its contravariant variable, so the two induced maps
compose into the one induced by `koszulCechComplexMap X f n ≫ cechAugmentation X f`. No
property of either map is used. -/
public theorem completionUnit_app_comp_map_koszulCechComplexMap
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))
    (n : ℕ) :
    (completionUnit X f).app K ≫
        ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).flip.obj K).map
          (DerivedCategory.Q.map (koszulCechComplexMap X f n)).op =
      (derivedStructureSheafHomIso X K).inv ≫
        ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).map
          (DerivedCategory.Q.map (koszulCechComplexMap X f n ≫ cechAugmentation X f)).op).app K :=
  (congrArg (fun w ↦ w ≫ ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).flip.obj K).map
        (DerivedCategory.Q.map (koszulCechComplexMap X f n)).op)
      (completionUnit_app X f K)).trans
    ((Category.assoc _ _ _).trans
      (congrArg (fun w ↦ (derivedStructureSheafHomIso X K).inv ≫ w)
        (congrArg (fun t ↦ NatTrans.app t K)
          ((((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).map_comp
                (DerivedCategory.Q.map (cechAugmentation X f)).op
                (DerivedCategory.Q.map (koszulCechComplexMap X f n)).op).symm).trans
            (congrArg (derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).map
              (congrArg Quiver.Hom.op
                (DerivedCategory.Q.map_comp (koszulCechComplexMap X f n)
                  (cechAugmentation X f)).symm))))))

/-- **The cone of the pinned Koszul presentation along the completion unit.** The completion unit
`K ⟶ K^∧` followed by the `n`-th projection of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite`
`.isDerivedLimitWithProjections_tensorDerivedDualSystem_koszulPowerSystem_completion` is the
identification `K = R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪, K)`, followed by the map which the composite
`K^n ⟶ Č(f) ⟶ 𝒪[0]` of the Koszul–Čech comparison with the Čech augmentation induces on derived
internal Hom into `K`, followed by the tower identification.

A map out of `K^∧` into a derived-complete object is determined by its restriction along the
unit, so this identity pins the projections themselves — and the right-hand side mentions neither
the Čech complex nor a homotopy colimit, only the map of complexes `K^n ⟶ 𝒪[0]`. -/
public theorem completionUnit_app_comp_tensorDerivedDualSystem_π
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))
    (n : ℕ) :
    (completionUnit X f).app K ≫
        (((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).flip.obj K).map
            (DerivedCategory.Q.map (koszulCechComplexMap X f n)).op ≫
          (koszulTensorDualSystemIso X f K).inv.app (op n)) =
      (derivedStructureSheafHomIso X K).inv ≫
        ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).map
            (DerivedCategory.Q.map (koszulCechComplexMap X f n ≫ cechAugmentation X f)).op).app K ≫
          (koszulTensorDualSystemIso X f K).inv.app (op n) :=
  (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans
    ((congrArg (fun w ↦ w ≫ (koszulTensorDualSystemIso X f K).inv.app (op n))
        (completionUnit_app_comp_map_koszulCechComplexMap X f K n)).trans
      (Category.assoc _ _ _))

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

end
